<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n24672" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭn-unguo</span></b>  (not <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">-go</span></b> ), unxi, unctum, 3, v.
		a., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to
			anoint</i> (<b>poet.</b> and in post-Aug. prose).
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<b>Lit.</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">oculos,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. L. L. 5, 8</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">non tamen idcirco contemnas lippus inungui,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor. Ep. 1, 1, 29</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. S. 1, 3, 25</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 28,
				9, 37, § 141</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">inunguendum primo lenibus,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					7, 7, 3</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> In
			gen., <i>to besmear</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lentem siccatam oleo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					18, 30, 73, § 308</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">id. 13, 3, 4, § 23 al.</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">conchis inuncta,</span>”
				<i>dressed with oil</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Mart.
					7, 78, 2</span></i>
			.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
